@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Analyze and retain one new public test — successful path
hide footbox
autonumber
participant "FrancAnalyzer / api.ts\n<<browser functions>>" as UI
participant "analyzer_api.py\nrecord_test() / test_view()" as API
participant "public_access.py\nrequire_shared_grammar()" as Guard
participant "analyzer_history.py\nrecord_test()" as History
participant "Compiler / analyzer.py\n<<functions>>" as Compiler
participant "store : PublicWorkspaceStore" as Store
activate UI
UI -> API : POST /api/analyzer/tests\n{request_id, exact text, saved grammar}
activate API
note over API : Public allowlist + Origin + CSRF + limit already passed.\ncourse_operation() holds the shared dataset lock for this operation.
API -> Guard : require_shared_grammar(grammar, request_id)
activate Guard
Guard -> Store : load_coursework() via load_project()
activate Store
Store --> Guard : saved grammar matches
deactivate Store
Guard --> API : allowed
deactivate Guard
API -> History : record_test(request)
activate History
History -> Store : load_analyzer_request(request_id)
activate Store
Store --> History : None (new request)
deactivate Store
History -> Compiler : analyze_grammar(request.grammar)
activate Compiler
Compiler --> History : transforms, sets, table, conflicts
deactivate Compiler
History -> Store : load_all() via dataset.load_all()
activate Store
Store --> History : Collection entries from the locked shared revision
deactivate Store
History -> Compiler : build_lexicon(entries);\nanalyze_manual(text, grammar, learned)
activate Compiler
Compiler --> History : exact lexical snapshot and parse result
deactivate Compiler
History -> Store : analyzer_test_identifier(request_id)
activate Store
Store --> History : stable actor-scoped UUID5 test ID
deactivate Store
note over History : RecordedTest.model_validate() captures text, grammar source,\nlexical/grammar/parse snapshots and exact-match metadata.
History -> Store : save_analyzer_request(request_id, record)
activate Store
note over Store : authorize_write(new analyzer_test) then INSERT snapshot\nand request mapping + bump version in one SQL transaction.
Store --> History : committed
deactivate Store
History --> API : immutable RecordedTest
deactivate History
API -> Store : ownership("analyzer_test", record.id)\nvia record_ownership()
activate Store
Store --> API : owner_id=null, owner_name="", can_edit=false
deactivate Store
note over API : test_view() derives VocabularyApproval from saved statistics.
API --> UI : OwnedRecordedTest with two distinct verdicts
deactivate API
UI -> UI : clear pendingTest; display result;\ninvalidate the saved-test report
activate UI
UI --> UI : ready for an intentional new test
deactivate UI
deactivate UI
legend bottom
  Storage calls abbreviate the real dataset/coursework_store/ownership ContextVar adapters.
  A retained grammar rejection is still a completed test; malformed/oversized grammar raises before insertion.
  No Collection entry, grammar, recording or private history is modified by this operation.
  Cancellation/timeout cannot promise rollback; identical retries are detailed separately.
endlegend
@enduml
